<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palencia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Palencia is a city on the Carrión river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and León, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, capital of the province of the same name. It succeeded the Vaccaean and Roman town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pallantia">Pallantia</a> and was restored as a bishopric in the 11th century. Around 1208 it received the first university of the Iberian peninsula, and its Gothic cathedral is known as 'the unknown beauty'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palencia.jpg" alt="Palencia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fernando Pascullo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palencia_Cathedral_2023_-_South_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Henry I of Castile, king at ten, died in 1217 aged thirteen after being struck on the head by a roof tile while playing with other boys at the bishop's palace in <b>Palencia</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>The Cantabri lived in the Cantabrian mountains and coast of northern Spain, in modern Cantabria and parts of Burgos, <b>Palencia</b> and León, from about the 4th century BCE.</blockquote><a href="/state/cantabri">Cantabri</a></li><li><blockquote>Around 943 Ramiro II of León created the County of Monzón, around Monzón de Campos near <b>Palencia</b>, for Assur Fernández, a rival of Fernán González of Castile.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-monzon">County of Monzón</a></li><li><blockquote>The Vaccaei occupied the middle Douro valley, in modern Valladolid, <b>Palencia</b>, Zamora and Burgos, from about the 4th century BCE.</blockquote><a href="/state/vaccaei">Vaccaei</a></li></ul></section>
